(OUT/'README.txt').write_text('Freeform nebula + illustrative layered galaxy /23October2026\n\nOpen review.html for six proof views; index.html is the standalone interactive study.\nA preserves actual Natural v5 map anchors/route. B is an explicitly illustrative600-marker fixture.\nGeneration influence ellipse is not a physical clip; separate padded XY bounds fade before edges; continuous depth-end fade remains proposed.\n\nTwo original32-slice fields,13.701s CPU /81.6MiB measured process peak.\nNo Unity/GPU/native input/build, portable taxonomy or generator/topology implementation.\nOfficial reference images were inspected but their pixels are not included.\n\nSource and updated plan are in source/. Reproduction recipes target the HobbyDS9 checkout\nand its preserved source-bound v1 map-context delivery; packaged viewing is self-contained.\nAll earlier galleries/builds/models remain unchanged.\n',encoding='utf-8')
(OUT/'review.html').write_text('''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Freeform nebulae and a layered galaxy</title><style>body{background:#050a12;color:#e7eaf3;font:18px Segoe UI;margin:30px;max-width:1700px}a{color:#9fd8fb}h1,h2{color:#efb16b;font-weight:500}p{line-height:1.5;max-width:1250px}img{width:100%;border:1px solid #43556b}.notice{background:#101c29;border-left:5px solid #efb16b;padding:18px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}</style><h1>Freeform clouds, shared space</h1><p><a href="index.html">Interactive depth study</a> · <a href="source/docs/art/freeform-nebula-galaxy.md">Updated Unity / taxonomy / generation plan</a> · <a href="independent-proof.json">Independent checks</a></p><div class="notice">Correction: supplied nebula radii describe generation influence, not physical or sensor extent. The revised cloud has independent padded bounds, broken wisps and cavities; it is not clipped to an ellipse. The previous gallery remains unchanged historical evidence.</div><h2>A · Original freeform nebula in the actual map</h2><img src="actual-freeform-centre.png" alt="Actual Natural v5 map with irregular original nebula"><p>Actual generic stars, regions and API-route presentation are unchanged.37.7–38.0% of sampled cloud alpha lies outside the generation ellipse. Source XY texture edges fade to zero inside separate padded bounds. Low residual depth-end alpha is disclosed in the plan; a continuous six-face fade is not proved here. Required markers/route stay above the cloud.</p><div class="grid"><section><h3>Pan left</h3><img src="actual-freeform-left.png" alt="Actual map and cloud panned left"></section><section><h3>Pan right</h3><img src="actual-freeform-right.png" alt="Actual map and cloud panned right"></section></div><h2>Generation influence diagnostic, not a shape boundary</h2><img src="freeform-depth-influence-diagnostic.png" alt="Freeform cloud extends beyond labelled generation influence ellipse"><p>Perspective near/far depth difference exceeds40px at120px pan; map-plane stars shift exactly240px across ±120px; flat-depth control0. Picking, compact layout, Play/Pause and immutable inputs passed. No new gameplay effect is implied by the wisps.</p><h2>B · Illustrative galaxy overview</h2><img src="illustrative-galaxy-overview.png" alt="Clearly labelled illustrative galaxy with600typed markers and local clouds"><p>This smooth structural sketch is a separate fixture, not current generated geography or finished Hubble-like galactic dust. It combines one diffuse3D field,600stellar/substellar glyphs and four transformed local-cloud instances. Classes and proportions are illustrative; the current backend still supplies generic stars.</p><h2>B · Regional view in the same coordinate system</h2><img src="illustrative-galaxy-regional.png" alt="Regional illustrative galaxy view showing typed stars and embedded freeform nebula"><p>Typed markers remain on the navigational reference plane; decorative fields have depth. Future portable taxonomy and macro-environment-first generation require separate versioned decisions and compatibility tests. Brown dwarfs are substellar; colours/glyph sizes are symbolic and never inferred from telescope pixels.</p><h2>Scope and provenance</h2><p>Two32×512×320fields generated on CPU in13.701s, measured process peak81.6MiB. Exactly six GPU-disabled headless captures; no extra polishing batch, Unity/import/build/native input, paid services or reference-pixel textures. Perspective depth planes are a bounded approximation, not arbitrary-orbit raymarching or a3D navigation model. GPU/LOD/memory targets in the plan are proposed, not measured acceptance.</p><p><a href="generation.json">Generation receipt</a> · <a href="browser-review.json">Browser proof</a> · <a href="reference-provenance.json">Inspected official references</a> · <a href="payload-manifest.json">Payload hashes</a></p></html>''',encoding='utf-8')
pin=subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],cwd=ROOT,text=True).strip();payload=[{'file':str(p.relative_to(OUT)).replace('\\','/'),'bytes':p.stat().st_size,'sha256':sha(p)} for p in sorted(OUT.rglob('*')) if p.is_file()]
manifest=OUT/'payload-manifest.json';manifest.write_text(json.dumps(payload,indent=2),encoding='utf-8');archive=OUT/'HobbyDS9-Freeform-Nebula-Galaxy-v2.zip'
